# q4_starve
Task 4.3  a request at cylinder 183 against a stream at 60
5000 stream requests, one every 1.0 ms, service 2.0 ms per request

algo   |   served |       wait | result
-------+----------+------------+------------------------
SSTF   |     5000 |    10002.0 ms | served
SCAN   |        0 |        2.0 ms | served
C-LOOK |        0 |        2.0 ms | served

SSTF always takes the request nearest to the head, so the steady
stream at 60 keeps the head at 60 and the request at 183 is never
the nearest one: it starves.  SCAN and C-LOOK sweep the disk, so
every cylinder is reached after a bounded number of requests.
